# Text files are checked out with LF on every system. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would
# turn the clone's files into CRLF: install.sh and .githooks/pre-commit would not run (sh reads "\r" as part of a
# word), and tests/golden/ would differ from what the tool prints (LF) in every answer. The files are LF in the
# repository already (git ls-files --eol), so this changes nothing on macOS or Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files, so that no line-ending rule ever touches them.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.exe binary
